      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "panel",
      "description": "Bounded evidence or ledger surface with one depth cue.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-panel\"><h3>Incident record</h3><p>Evidence remains attached to time.</p></section>",
      "css": ".ds-panel{padding:24px;border:1px solid oklch(var(--line));border-radius:14px;background:oklch(var(--panel));color:oklch(var(--ink));font:400 14px/1.5 'IBM Plex Sans',sans-serif}.ds-panel h3{margin:0 0 8px;font:600 18px/1.4 Outfit,sans-serif}.ds-panel p{margin:0;color:oklch(var(--muted))}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Causal Trace",
      "kind": "custom",
      "description": "Signature time-and-service instrument with a selected orange playhead.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-trace\"><span class=\"ds-trace-label\">inventory-api</span><i></i><b></b><em></em></div>",
      "css": ".ds-trace{position:relative;height:112px;overflow:hidden;border-radius:14px;background-color:oklch(var(--elevated));background-image:linear-gradient(to right,oklch(var(--line)/.34) 1px,transparent 1px),linear-gradient(to bottom,oklch(var(--line)/.22) 1px,transparent 1px);background-size:32px 32px;color:oklch(var(--muted));font:500 11px 'JetBrains Mono',monospace}.ds-trace-label{position:absolute;left:16px;top:18px}.ds-trace i{position:absolute;left:16px;right:16px;top:48px;height:1px;background:oklch(var(--line))}.ds-trace b{position:absolute;left:48%;top:40px;width:16px;height:16px;border:2px solid oklch(var(--accent));border-radius:9999px;background:oklch(var(--accent)/.3);box-shadow:0 0 0 7px oklch(var(--accent)/.12)}.ds-trace em{position:absolute;left:calc(48% + 7px);top:14px;bottom:12px;width:1px;background:oklch(var(--accent))}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Industrial Chronograph Bench",
    "overview": "ReplayOps feels like a calibrated instrument used under pressure: precise, legible, and deliberately quieter than the event it is helping diagnose. The system is dense where evidence needs comparison and breathable around decisions. It rejects neon observability spectacle and generic AI-chat styling; assistant output is visually subordinate to the incident record.",
    "keyCharacteristics": ["Evidence-first hierarchy with the causal trace as the focal instrument.", "Cool hue-tinted neutrals in both light and dark themes.", "Sparse incident orange reserved for high-intent controls and active time.", "Human-readable operational copy paired with monospaced measurements.", "Restrained spring motion only where spatial continuity matters."],
    "rules": [
      { "name": "The Ten-Percent Signal Rule", "body": "Incident Orange occupies no more than roughly one tenth of a screen; its scarcity makes an active control or time marker immediately legible.", "section": "colors" },
      { "name": "The Tinted Neutral Rule", "body": "Every neutral carries the primary blue hue. Unrelated pure gray, pure black, and pure white do not enter the interface.", "section": "colors" },
      { "name": "The Measurement Reserve Rule", "body": "Monospace belongs only to time, identity, code-like evidence, and numeric measurement.", "section": "typography" },
      { "name": "The One Depth Cue Rule", "body": "A resting surface earns a border or a shadow, not both.", "section": "elevation" }
    ],
    "dos": ["Do lead incident surfaces with evidence and time, then place summaries around them.", "Do use semantic OKLCH tokens and keep neutrals inside the blue instrument family.", "Do label synthetic values, AI uncertainty, and human-approval boundaries explicitly.", "Do retain 44px touch targets, visible focus, reduced-motion behavior, and text alternatives for charts."],
    "donts": ["Don't use Inter, Roboto, generic purple-to-blue gradients, gradient text, pure black, or pure white-on-gray nesting.", "Don't turn every metric into a card, add decorative sparklines, or nest framed panels without a real information boundary.", "Don't use the trace grid, cross-hatching, or monospaced type as ambient decoration.", "Don't make AI answers visually outrank the evidence that grounds them."]
  }
